    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78626" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραπόλλυμι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>destroy, consume</i> or <i>spend to no purpose,
				waste, lose</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸναῦλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.439e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				12.5
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καιρόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Charito
					1.7
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡλικίαν τὴν ἐκ τῆς Ἰταλίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					74.2
				</span></i>
			 :—more freq. in 
				Med.
			 and 
				Pass.
			, with pf.
			<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραπόλωλα</span>, <i>perish</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραπολεῖ βοώμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					1228
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραπόλωλεν ἡ τέχνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dionys.
				</span></i>
			 Com.<i><span class="en">
				2.35
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠτίμωται καὶ παραπόλωλεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.91
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκαρὴς παραπόλωλας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					835
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ βίος μελλησμῷ παραπόλλυται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Sent. Vat.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμῷ παραπολοῦμαι</span>”
